  "footnote": "Students who matriculated before Fall 2025 must consult their History of Art advisor about major requirement options. The checklist follows the current catalog: 10 courses, at least 6 at the 3000-level or above. FWS courses do not count. Optional honors requires ARTH 4998 and ARTH 4999; only ARTH 4999 counts as a major elective, so honors requires at least 11 courses. Honors also requires satisfactory major progress, the Knight Institute Honors Writing Workshop, a symposium presentation and a thesis defense; discuss plans and a thesis advisor in spring of junior year. A prior formal research paper and junior-year ARTH 4101 are recommended.",
